   "content": "PolyStrata is a local inference engine for running large mixture-of-experts language models on consumer hardware. It targets Qwen3.8-Flash-Next and its variants, which use a hybrid of linear attention (GDN) and standard attention layers with a large expert pool. The engine's core idea is to keep as many experts as possible in GPU VRAM, stream the rest over PCIe, and compute whatever the GPU cannot hold on the CPU in parallel, so that a 12 GB card can serve a model whose full expert set would need 34\u201350 GB of RAM.\n\n**Speed.** On a reference PC (RTX 5070 12 GB, Ryzen 5 7600, 64 GB DDR5), the Q2_0 quantization processes a 4K prompt at roughly 1,294 tokens/s and generates output at about 93 tokens/s. At 128K context, prompt speed holds near 2,100 tokens/s while output drops to 74 tokens/s. The IQ2_XS variant is slightly slower on prompts but comparable on output. A Coder variant (half the experts, pruned for code) runs prompts at up to 2,200 tokens/s. Engine 0.1.36 added fused int8 tensor-core kernels for prompt processing on RTX 30 and newer cards, gaining 16\u201322% over 0.1.26, and thread-block-cluster decode kernels on RTX 50 that push Q2_0 output from 89 to 93.5 tokens/s at 4K. On AMD, an RX 7900 XTX with a tuned ROCm build reaches 1,641 prompt and 64 output tokens/s at 32K with IQ3_S.\n\n**Model choices.** Three main quantizations are offered: Q2_0 (66 GB download, ~34 GB RAM, fastest), IQ2_XS (68 GB, ~36 GB RAM, slightly better quality), and IQ3_XXS (76 GB, ~43 GB RAM, best quality but slower due to more CPU work). All three fit on a 64 GB machine. A Coder variant with half the experts runs on 32 GB RAM and targets code tasks. Swift 1.5 is a fine-tune that produces shorter thinking chains (63% fewer thinking tokens) at the same inference speed. An experimental 4-bit Unsloth quantization (UD-Q4_K_XL, 72 GiB of experts) runs at 7\u20138.5 tokens/s on a 64 GB PC by reading most experts from the SSD.\n\n**System requirements.** An NVIDIA RTX 20/30/40/50 series GPU with at least 12 GB VRAM (8 GB works but slowly), or supported AMD Radeon cards via HIP. 64 GB RAM is recommended. The CPU needs AVX2; AVX-512 gives a modest boost. Disk space of 70\u201380 GB for the model plus ~6 GB for the MTP draft layer. Windows 10/11 or Linux (Ubuntu, Debian) are supported; WSL works with a limitation that KV streaming is unavailable.\n\n**Installation.** On Windows, double-clicking START-HERE.bat asks four questions (which model family, which size, context length, images yes/no) and then downloads, configures, and starts everything. A browser opens to a local web app at port 8080 with four tabs: Chat (streaming answers with thinking display), Monitor (GPU/CPU/RAM metrics and request log), Requests (API monitor), and About. On Linux, ./setup.sh does the same. The model files live in a data folder next to the PolyStrata directory, so updates do not re-download them.\n\n**Key",
